# Zed writes settings by atomic replace, and it canonicalizes the symlink first,
# so its temp file gets created next to the *real* target -- in here. A crash
# mid-write leaves one behind, and `git cia` would commit it without asking.
#
# Deliberately not in config/zed/, since link_tree finds every file under
# config/ and would symlink this into ~/.config/zed/.
config/zed/.tmp*
